WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:01.252 --> 00:00:03.379
[dramatic music playing]

2
00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:06.298
[man] Ben! Ethan! Wake up. ya goldbricks!

3
00:00:06.382 --> 00:00:08.467
I got donuts!

4
00:00:08.551 --> 00:00:10.136
Homemade?

5
00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:13.431
Why would they be homemade?
Who makes donuts at home?

6
00:00:13.514 --> 00:00:15.683
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[whoosh]

7
00:00:17.435 --> 00:00:19.019
[whooshing continues]

8
00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:24.900
[loud banging]

9
00:00:24.984 --> 00:00:26.318
What in the hell?

10
00:00:27.403 --> 00:00:29.572
[mechanical voice]
Triad Industries is under attack.

11
00:00:29.655 --> 00:00:31.449
You are not the targets.

12
00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:34.493
For your own safety. get out. now.

13
00:00:34.577 --> 00:00:35.786
[grunts]

14
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.915
[panting and groaning]

15
00:00:39.999 --> 00:00:41.959
[suspenseful music playing]

16
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

17
00:00:50.009 --> 00:00:52.887
[whooshing]

18
00:00:55.765 --> 00:00:57.933
[theme music playing]

19
00:01:27.588 --> 00:01:29.507
[dramatic music playing]

20
00:01:33.928 --> 00:01:37.181
[Pennyworth]
Now. that is the definition of a rum do.

21
00:01:37.264 --> 00:01:39.892
At least there were no casualties.
That’s something.

22
00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:43.938
One wonders what was inside
that might cause such an explosion.

23
00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:46.273
The Express says "electrical fire."

24
00:01:46.357 --> 00:01:48.818
Confined to three of the uppermost floors?

25
00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:51.570
In a building containing
no industrial equipment?

26
00:01:51.654 --> 00:01:53.572
Don’t you find that odd?

27
00:01:53.656 --> 00:01:56.908
What's odd is either of you
caring about this at all.

28
00:01:56.991 --> 00:01:59.119
If the papers are saying
it’s an accident.

29
00:01:59.203 --> 00:02:01.080
GCPD must’ve signed off.

30
00:02:01.831 --> 00:02:02.915
I don't know.

31
00:02:02.998 --> 00:02:05.417
There are an awful lot
of unanswered questions.

32
00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:08.169
Why are you here on a Saturday. Lucius?

33
00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:10.214
Do you ever stop working?

34
00:02:10.297 --> 00:02:13.175
Today is Monday. and that means...

35
00:02:13.259 --> 00:02:14.677
paperwork.

36
00:02:15.845 --> 00:02:17.972
Monday? Really?

37
00:02:20.015 --> 00:02:21.892
Triad Industries?

38
00:02:21.976 --> 00:02:23.602
Do I know that name?

39
00:02:23.686 --> 00:02:27.356
The CEOs approached
your company for funding. Rejected.

40
00:02:27.439 --> 00:02:30.150
I remember.
They gave some kind of presentation.

41
00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:32.278
A new power source?

42
00:02:32.361 --> 00:02:35.281
Ultrium.
They had documents and a pitch reel.

43
00:02:35.364 --> 00:02:36.824
All still at my office.

44
00:02:36.906 --> 00:02:39.535
Great. Bring everything along tomorrow.

45
00:02:39.618 --> 00:02:42.704
We’ll screen it in the theater.
Pennyworth can make popcorn!

46
00:02:42.788 --> 00:02:44.874
And why am I doing this?

47
00:02:44.957 --> 00:02:47.877
What? I'm taking an active hand.

48
00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:51.589
[dramatic music playing]

49
00:02:57.511 --> 00:02:59.305
Pennyworth. I'm inside.

50
00:03:00.598 --> 00:03:04.018
I hear you. sir.
My notepad is at the ready.

51
00:03:05.102 --> 00:03:09.106
The Express undersold it.
No way an electrical fire caused this.

52
00:03:12.693 --> 00:03:14.028
These look like...

53
00:03:14.111 --> 00:03:15.613
blast craters.

54
00:03:16.155 --> 00:03:19.074
They appear to be
from simultaneous explosions.

55
00:03:19.158 --> 00:03:22.328
[Pennyworth. over device]
As in grenades or bombs?

56
00:03:22.411 --> 00:03:24.413
Inconclusive. I need to look at--

57
00:03:24.496 --> 00:03:27.416
You've done a good job
keeping a lid on things. Sal.

58
00:03:27.499 --> 00:03:29.668
Thanks. Mr. Hardwick. sir.

59
00:03:29.752 --> 00:03:33.839
But I was thinkin' maybe we let
the cops in on what's been happening?

60
00:03:33.923 --> 00:03:36.175
Let the partners decide
what we can handle.

61
00:03:36.258 --> 00:03:38.802
You just keep doing
what you've been doing.

62
00:03:38.886 --> 00:03:40.387
Keeping a lid on things.

63
00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:44.141
What is that?

64
00:03:45.142 --> 00:03:47.061
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[both gasp]

65
00:03:47.144 --> 00:03:49.355
[grunting]

66
00:03:49.438 --> 00:03:50.481
[groaning]

67
00:03:51.607 --> 00:03:52.441
[grunts]

68
00:03:57.488 --> 00:03:59.490
[dramatic music playing]

69
00:04:04.745 --> 00:04:07.831
-[projector whirring]
-[classical music playing]

70
00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:17.591
[woman] All over the world.
people are starving.

71
00:04:17.675 --> 00:04:20.803
Epidemics kill millions across the globe.

72
00:04:20.886 --> 00:04:24.765
Nations wage war over territory
and resources.

73
00:04:24.848 --> 00:04:29.561
Generation after generation.
century after century.

74
00:04:29.645 --> 00:04:33.023
Is humanity fated to repeat
these horrors forever?

75
00:04:33.107 --> 00:04:34.900
I say. “no.”

76
00:04:34.984 --> 00:04:36.652
Not if we look up.

77
00:04:36.735 --> 00:04:39.196
Our future is in the stars.

78
00:04:39.822 --> 00:04:41.240
Exploration.

79
00:04:41.323 --> 00:04:42.950
Invention.

80
00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:46.787
This future is made possible by
my new rocket-based technology.

81
00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:51.291
and by Ultrium. the fuel of the future.

82
00:04:51.375 --> 00:04:54.795
Clean. pure. inexhaustible.

83
00:04:54.878 --> 00:04:58.382
The perfect power for a golden destiny.

84
00:04:58.465 --> 00:05:02.970
It’s time for humanity to blast off!

85
00:05:03.053 --> 00:05:05.556
Why did we pass on this again?

86
00:05:05.639 --> 00:05:08.392
Misters Lydecker. Lawford. and Hardwick
wouldn’t let us

87
00:05:08.475 --> 00:05:12.271
independently evaluate Ultrium and
the designs for their rocket technology.

88
00:05:12.354 --> 00:05:15.024
Am I sensing a change of mind on Triad?

89
00:05:15.107 --> 00:05:18.318
Let's just say. my interest is peaked.

90
00:05:18.402 --> 00:05:20.696
You wanna take another look
at this project?

91
00:05:20.779 --> 00:05:22.531
See how far along they are?

92
00:05:22.614 --> 00:05:23.741
I do.

93
00:05:23.824 --> 00:05:27.202
I like this version of you. Bruce.
Participation suits you.

94
00:05:27.286 --> 00:05:28.537
I’ll set up a meeting.

95
00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.956
I don't know why I set up this meeting.

96
00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.249
You never come to meetings.

97
00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:34.793
You have no idea how things
are supposed to go.

98
00:05:34.877 --> 00:05:38.380
Don’t worry. I went to the same school
as you. remember?

99
00:05:39.089 --> 00:05:40.924
[man] Gentlemen!

100
00:05:41.008 --> 00:05:44.094
Warren Lawford. CEO of Triad Industries.

101
00:05:44.178 --> 00:05:47.723
Good to see you again.
And this is Bruce Wayne.

102
00:05:47.806 --> 00:05:50.768
Of course it is. A pure pleasure. sir.

103
00:05:50.851 --> 00:05:52.436
We've got so much to show you.

104
00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.814
Thank you for taking this meeting
on such short notice.

105
00:05:55.898 --> 00:05:58.776
Nonsense.
We welcome your renewed interest.

106
00:05:58.859 --> 00:06:02.488
-You gave us the high hat last time.
-Hardwick. is it?

107
00:06:02.571 --> 00:06:06.075
It’s Lucius’s job to zealously
protect my assets.

108
00:06:06.158 --> 00:06:07.242
And I do.

109
00:06:07.326 --> 00:06:11.080
But I couldn’t get your Ultrium project
out of my mind.

110
00:06:11.163 --> 00:06:13.957
I know exactly what you mean. Mr. Wayne.

111
00:06:14.041 --> 00:06:15.584
Ultrium is a miracle element.

112
00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:19.379
Nearly unlimited power generated
by even the tiniest amounts.

113
00:06:19.463 --> 00:06:21.173
Amazing.

114
00:06:21.256 --> 00:06:25.260
Honestly. I was hoping to meet with
Dr. Sutton. Her designs are incredible.

115
00:06:25.344 --> 00:06:29.056
A genius like our Roxy comes along
once in a generation. [chuckles]

116
00:06:29.139 --> 00:06:32.976
The world will sing her praises
for centuries to come. but--

117
00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.645
Sutton's dead.

118
00:06:35.187 --> 00:06:37.314
[man] Lucius Fox.

119
00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:39.817
Hello. again. Long time.

120
00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:45.072
Armand Lydecker. meet Bruce Wayne.
We’re giving Ultrium another look.

121
00:06:45.155 --> 00:06:47.074
So Warren said.

122
00:06:47.157 --> 00:06:49.534
So... Dr. Sutton?

123
00:06:49.618 --> 00:06:51.787
Oh. you're talking about Roxy.

124
00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:54.373
You see. there was... an accident.

125
00:06:54.456 --> 00:06:56.834
An explosion at her home lab.

126
00:06:56.917 --> 00:07:00.337
Tragic. Killed instantly. the poor girl.

127
00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.964
Nothing left of her at all.

128
00:07:02.047 --> 00:07:04.049
[tense music playing]

129
00:07:06.051 --> 00:07:08.470
[Lydecker] The important thing
is most of Roxy’s notes.

130
00:07:08.554 --> 00:07:10.931
her designs were copied
prior to her death.

131
00:07:11.014 --> 00:07:13.350
Enough to make sure her legacy survives.

132
00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:15.853
We’ll use it to usher in a new golden age.

133
00:07:15.936 --> 00:07:18.313
That’s... commendable.

134
00:07:19.189 --> 00:07:21.984
[Bruce] This prototype really
is impressive.

135
00:07:22.067 --> 00:07:24.111
The project's in its final phase?

136
00:07:24.194 --> 00:07:26.196
Even without Dr. Sutton?

137
00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:28.991
Losing Roxy was a blow.

138
00:07:29.074 --> 00:07:31.785
But yes. we’re actually ahead of schedule.

139
00:07:31.869 --> 00:07:35.289
We’re demonstrating our working
rocket prototype this weekend.

140
00:07:35.372 --> 00:07:39.126
Think of it. A projectile as big
as an office building.

141
00:07:39.209 --> 00:07:42.129
powered by a single brick of Ultrium!

142
00:07:42.212 --> 00:07:44.214
We’d love for you to attend
our little demo.

143
00:07:44.298 --> 00:07:46.508
Just us. a few foreign dignitaries.

144
00:07:46.592 --> 00:07:50.220
-and people with money and vision.
-[dramatic music playing]

145
00:07:50.304 --> 00:07:51.847
We're taking no chances.

146
00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:55.808
The Ultrium will travel by rail to be
stored at a secure Triad testing site.

147
00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:57.895
[Lawford] Nothing will stop the launch.

148
00:07:57.978 --> 00:08:00.981
A squad of Gunther’s best men will be
on guard the whole time.

149
00:08:04.234 --> 00:08:06.236
[dramatic music continues]

150
00:08:12.409 --> 00:08:14.411
[train horn blaring]

151
00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.371
[rocket whooshing]

152
00:08:16.455 --> 00:08:18.540
[suspenseful music playing]

153
00:08:21.043 --> 00:08:23.045
[horn blaring continues]

154
00:08:25.881 --> 00:08:27.758
A lot of fuss for a shiny brick. huh?

155
00:08:29.885 --> 00:08:31.220
What the hell?

156
00:08:31.303 --> 00:08:33.222
[loud banging]

157
00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.102
[suspenseful music continues]

158
00:08:43.023 --> 00:08:44.566
[grunting]

159
00:08:48.987 --> 00:08:50.906
[suspenseful music continues]

160
00:08:58.538 --> 00:08:59.706
[grunts]

161
00:09:02.709 --> 00:09:03.835
Another one!

162
00:09:05.003 --> 00:09:06.088
[grunting]

163
00:09:08.131 --> 00:09:09.424
[groans]

164
00:09:11.718 --> 00:09:14.137
[grunts and groans]

165
00:09:16.014 --> 00:09:17.015
[yells]

166
00:09:19.351 --> 00:09:20.936
[grunting]

167
00:09:22.854 --> 00:09:23.689
[groans]

168
00:09:26.441 --> 00:09:27.276
[grunts]

169
00:09:28.735 --> 00:09:29.820
[groans]

170
00:09:32.364 --> 00:09:33.365
[Batman] Dr. Sutton?

171
00:09:33.699 --> 00:09:34.908
[suit whirring]

172
00:09:34.992 --> 00:09:35.826
[groans]

173
00:09:37.035 --> 00:09:37.869
[grunts]

174
00:09:51.216 --> 00:09:53.218
[tense music playing]

175
00:09:58.307 --> 00:10:00.434
[tense music continues]

176
00:10:10.444 --> 00:10:11.945
[tires squealing]

177
00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.370
[tires screeching]

178
00:10:20.454 --> 00:10:22.456
[rocket whooshing in distance]

179
00:10:24.082 --> 00:10:26.084
[dramatic music playing]

180
00:10:31.006 --> 00:10:32.924
[Batman] I saw her. Pennyworth.

181
00:10:33.008 --> 00:10:36.428
Four Triad locations destroyed
in the last year.

182
00:10:36.511 --> 00:10:38.972
[Pennyworth]
And not the result of accidents.

183
00:10:39.056 --> 00:10:40.807
One? Accident.

184
00:10:40.891 --> 00:10:42.559
Two? Coincidence.

185
00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:45.604
Three. four. five now with the train.

186
00:10:45.687 --> 00:10:49.232
There’s a six month gap between
the destruction at Dr. Sutton’s home lab

187
00:10:49.316 --> 00:10:50.692
and the first--

188
00:10:50.776 --> 00:10:53.779
Are we calling them attacks officially?

189
00:10:53.862 --> 00:10:55.989
Followed by the machine warehouse.

190
00:10:56.073 --> 00:10:57.991
Now. this recent attack on the train.

191
00:10:58.075 --> 00:10:59.951
and at the Triad home office.

192
00:11:00.035 --> 00:11:02.829
[Batman] Only their records library
was destroyed.

193
00:11:02.913 --> 00:11:05.665
Patents. blueprints. formulas.

194
00:11:05.749 --> 00:11:08.418
You believe Dr. Sutton
is responsible for all of it.

195
00:11:08.502 --> 00:11:10.545
[Batman] This was caused
by small explosions.

196
00:11:10.629 --> 00:11:13.173
the kind made
by that rocket pistol of hers.

197
00:11:13.256 --> 00:11:16.385
She's using her inventions
to damage Triad.

198
00:11:16.468 --> 00:11:17.886
Curious.

199
00:11:17.969 --> 00:11:21.848
Why go to these lengths?
Why fake her own death?

200
00:11:21.932 --> 00:11:23.558
Too many questions.

201
00:11:24.059 --> 00:11:26.561
But I've got an idea
where to get some answers.

202
00:11:27.646 --> 00:11:29.648
[dramatic music playing]

203
00:11:36.905 --> 00:11:38.448
[doors creak open]

204
00:11:38.532 --> 00:11:40.534
[tense music playing]

205
00:11:50.585 --> 00:11:51.920
[creaking]

206
00:11:52.003 --> 00:11:54.047
[doors scrape open]

207
00:12:06.393 --> 00:12:08.395
[dramatic music playing]

208
00:12:11.606 --> 00:12:13.984
[Batman] You have to stop this.
Dr. Sutton.

209
00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:16.528
[Sutton] You shouldn't have come here.

210
00:12:16.611 --> 00:12:18.155
You haven’t killed anyone yet.

211
00:12:18.238 --> 00:12:21.324
But your luck will run out.
This vendetta can’t go on--

212
00:12:21.408 --> 00:12:25.287
[Sutton] The masked vigilante
is lecturing me about vendettas?

213
00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:27.289
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[Sutton groans]

214
00:12:27.372 --> 00:12:28.373
[grunts]

215
00:12:29.458 --> 00:12:33.253
You need help.
The accident obviously hurt your mind.

216
00:12:33.336 --> 00:12:35.338
Accident? It was them.

217
00:12:35.422 --> 00:12:38.800
I found out what those animals
were doing with my work!

218
00:12:39.342 --> 00:12:41.678
You’re trying to sell my plans
to foreign powers!

219
00:12:41.761 --> 00:12:44.055
Dr. Sutton. Roxy...

220
00:12:44.139 --> 00:12:45.307
be reasonable.

221
00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:48.185
Rockets to the stars cost money.
This is how we--

222
00:12:48.268 --> 00:12:50.270
You've breached our contract!

223
00:12:51.021 --> 00:12:52.856
You'll be hearing from my lawyer.

224
00:12:54.483 --> 00:12:56.485
[dramatic music playing]

225
00:13:09.414 --> 00:13:11.666
[suspenseful music playing]

226
00:13:12.083 --> 00:13:12.918
[gasps]

227
00:13:17.923 --> 00:13:19.925
[dramatic music playing]

228
00:13:40.862 --> 00:13:44.032
When I discovered their plans for my work.

229
00:13:44.115 --> 00:13:46.493
they tried to remove me.

230
00:13:46.576 --> 00:13:48.411
If that’s true. they’re criminals.

231
00:13:48.495 --> 00:13:51.373
I can get to the bottom of it.
Bring them to justice.

232
00:13:51.456 --> 00:13:55.377
Where were you when they were
corrupting my work?

233
00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:58.255
Where were you when they tried to kill me?

234
00:14:01.091 --> 00:14:02.133
[Batman groans]

235
00:14:09.516 --> 00:14:11.184
[suspenseful music playing]

236
00:14:14.312 --> 00:14:15.230
[groans]

237
00:14:21.403 --> 00:14:23.405
[dramatic music playing]

238
00:14:24.489 --> 00:14:27.450
-[Batman] Sutton's obsessed. Pennyworth.
-And so I gather. sir.

239
00:14:27.534 --> 00:14:31.538
Her campaign seems to have been
quite successful thus far.

240
00:14:31.621 --> 00:14:34.415
This testing facility
is the last place left.

241
00:14:34.499 --> 00:14:36.543
She'll certainly attack it then.

242
00:14:36.626 --> 00:14:40.964
The demonstration is tomorrow.
There’ll be guests. company personnel.

243
00:14:41.464 --> 00:14:44.384
In situations like this.
many would call in the police.

244
00:14:44.467 --> 00:14:46.553
Perhaps warn Commissioner Gordon
of the impending--

245
00:14:46.636 --> 00:14:48.346
Gordon's people can't handle her.

246
00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:51.099
With her technology.
she'd cut through them like butter.

247
00:14:51.182 --> 00:14:52.684
Then it's down to you...

248
00:14:52.767 --> 00:14:54.019
again.

249
00:14:54.603 --> 00:14:57.439
But the testing ground
is hundreds of miles from Gotham.

250
00:14:58.523 --> 00:15:00.900
However will you get there in time?

251
00:15:00.984 --> 00:15:02.986
[dramatic music playing]

252
00:15:06.531 --> 00:15:10.493
[Lawford] The rocket is a magnificent
example of Triad technology.

253
00:15:10.577 --> 00:15:13.330
but the real miracle is the power source.

254
00:15:13.413 --> 00:15:17.834
Ultrium is clean. reusable.
and easy to produce.

255
00:15:17.917 --> 00:15:22.255
That behemoth is powered by a cube
no bigger than a paperweight.

256
00:15:22.339 --> 00:15:24.507
Welcome to the future.
ladies and gentleman.

257
00:15:24.591 --> 00:15:26.676
It’s one you will own.

258
00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:28.970
At wholesale prices.

259
00:15:29.387 --> 00:15:31.723
[clapping]

260
00:15:31.806 --> 00:15:33.808
[dramatic music playing]

261
00:15:43.943 --> 00:15:46.363
At least try to grow a spine. Armand.

262
00:15:46.446 --> 00:15:47.572
Don't you get it?

263
00:15:47.656 --> 00:15:51.826
What’s in the rocket is our last cube
of Ultrium. If the test fails--

264
00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:54.454
Your whining is starting
to get on my nerves!

265
00:15:55.205 --> 00:15:57.915
-Stop it. Both of you.
-Let’s call it off. Warren.

266
00:15:57.999 --> 00:16:00.627
We can say
there were technical difficulties.

267
00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.504
Call them all back in a few months.

268
00:16:02.587 --> 00:16:03.880
“Call them all back?”

269
00:16:03.963 --> 00:16:06.424
They won’t come!
This is our only chance!

270
00:16:06.549 --> 00:16:09.094
All our assets are tied
to today’s success.

271
00:16:09.177 --> 00:16:13.390
Once they see what we have.
we’ll be awash in government contracts.

272
00:16:13.473 --> 00:16:15.767
Private investment. Trust me.

273
00:16:16.309 --> 00:16:17.769
Roxy's still out there!

274
00:16:17.852 --> 00:16:22.774
Relax. Even if she does show. this time
my boys are ready for anything she’s got.

275
00:16:23.358 --> 00:16:25.402
See? Everything’s going to plan.

276
00:16:26.611 --> 00:16:27.821
Right.

277
00:16:27.904 --> 00:16:29.239
Start the countdown!

278
00:16:29.322 --> 00:16:30.323
[beeps]

279
00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:35.412
[suspenseful music playing]

280
00:17:05.442 --> 00:17:07.986
[suspenseful music continues]

281
00:17:43.229 --> 00:17:44.647
[grunts]

282
00:17:44.731 --> 00:17:47.484
[grunting and groaning]

283
00:17:49.694 --> 00:17:50.653
[groans]

284
00:17:51.696 --> 00:17:52.739
[grunts]

285
00:17:53.323 --> 00:17:54.699
It's over. Dr. Sutton.

286
00:17:55.158 --> 00:17:56.910
Look around! [grunts]

287
00:17:56.993 --> 00:17:59.078
Don't you see where we are?

288
00:17:59.162 --> 00:18:02.457
[dramatic music playing]

289
00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:04.292
This is my work.

290
00:18:04.375 --> 00:18:05.752
Mine!

291
00:18:05.835 --> 00:18:08.296
They’re selling it to madmen!

292
00:18:08.379 --> 00:18:09.756
Mass murderers.

293
00:18:10.924 --> 00:18:13.885
They’ll turn the whole world
into a perpetual war z--

294
00:18:13.968 --> 00:18:14.928
[gunfire]

295
00:18:15.011 --> 00:18:17.013
[suspenseful music playing]

296
00:18:17.764 --> 00:18:20.058
It’s called "business." Roxy.

297
00:18:21.017 --> 00:18:22.936
Kill them! Kill them both!

298
00:18:26.231 --> 00:18:27.982
[groaning]

299
00:18:29.776 --> 00:18:31.236
[groaning]

300
00:18:37.617 --> 00:18:39.577
Why couldn't you just take the money?

301
00:18:39.661 --> 00:18:41.371
Let the men handle the business.

302
00:18:41.454 --> 00:18:43.998
I won't have that blood on my hands!

303
00:18:44.916 --> 00:18:46.084
[grunts]

304
00:18:47.252 --> 00:18:48.253
You see now?

305
00:18:48.336 --> 00:18:50.672
I’ve destroyed everything
they stole from me.

306
00:18:50.755 --> 00:18:52.549
All but one piece of Ultrium!

307
00:18:52.632 --> 00:18:54.050
The one in the rocket.

308
00:18:58.096 --> 00:19:00.932
I can rewire it. make sure the test fails.

309
00:19:01.015 --> 00:19:02.642
It’ll bankrupt Triad.

310
00:19:02.725 --> 00:19:04.185
[suspenseful music continues]

311
00:19:06.145 --> 00:19:07.063
[gun clicks]

312
00:19:07.146 --> 00:19:09.357
That's it. I'm out of ammo.

313
00:19:10.066 --> 00:19:10.900
I'm not.

314
00:19:12.944 --> 00:19:14.821
Warren! Launch the rocket!

315
00:19:14.904 --> 00:19:16.823
[Hardwick. over intercom]
Do you hear me? Launch!

316
00:19:16.906 --> 00:19:19.075
-Warren...
-Launch the rocket!

317
00:19:19.158 --> 00:19:22.078
Sir? We’re only halfway
through the countdown.

318
00:19:22.161 --> 00:19:24.539
-I said. "Launch." Now!
-[whimpers]

319
00:19:30.044 --> 00:19:32.046
[dramatic music playing]

320
00:19:48.813 --> 00:19:50.398
I'll deal with them. Go!

321
00:19:50.481 --> 00:19:53.651
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[grunting and groaning]

322
00:19:59.574 --> 00:20:01.951
[grunts and groans]

323
00:20:03.703 --> 00:20:04.787
[frustrated grunts]

324
00:20:11.794 --> 00:20:13.880
[groans and grunts]

325
00:20:15.715 --> 00:20:17.216
[groans]

326
00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:19.093
[grunting]

327
00:20:19.177 --> 00:20:20.803
[suspenseful music continues]

328
00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:25.099
[groans]

329
00:20:25.183 --> 00:20:26.517
[grunts and groans continue]

330
00:20:29.145 --> 00:20:31.147
[suspenseful music continues]

331
00:20:47.997 --> 00:20:49.457
[chuckling]

332
00:20:50.583 --> 00:20:52.210
Too late. freak!

333
00:20:52.293 --> 00:20:56.172
There's nothing she can do.
The demo will be a complete success!

334
00:20:56.255 --> 00:20:59.592
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[struggling. groaning]

335
00:21:01.219 --> 00:21:04.806
[dramatic music playing]

336
00:21:06.391 --> 00:21:07.809
[gasping]

337
00:21:09.435 --> 00:21:11.437
[pained groaning]

338
00:21:18.152 --> 00:21:20.113
[dramatic music playing]

339
00:21:38.548 --> 00:21:42.510
-Are you quite sure about this. sir?
-It's what she wanted.

340
00:21:42.593 --> 00:21:47.181
In the right hands.
Dr. Sutton's work could be transformative.

341
00:21:47.265 --> 00:21:49.267
And whose hands would that be?

342
00:21:53.521 --> 00:21:55.523
[emotional music playing]

343
00:22:16.377 --> 00:22:19.255
[ominous music playing]

344
00:22:19.338 --> 00:22:22.925
[man whistling tune]

345
00:22:31.142 --> 00:22:33.144
[whistling continues]

346
00:22:36.355 --> 00:22:38.357
[scary music playing]

347
00:22:42.779 --> 00:22:44.781
[credits music playing]

347
00:22:45.305 --> 00:23:45.404
